# Shell scripts must keep LF endings even when checked out on Windows.
#
# The readme tells Windows users to build the firmware in WSL, and a script with
# CRLF endings fails there with `bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M` - or, worse,
# survives the shebang and then breaks on a line continuation somewhere in the
# middle. Nothing on Windows needs these to be CRLF; bash is the only thing that
# reads them.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same argument, for the same reason: WSL runs these.
tools/* text eol=lf
